% 12. Five children: the gross income limit rises by £222, but the
% household is still over it.
scenario large_family_over_gross is:
    olga is a client.
    olga applies for "legal representation".
    the age of olga is 36.
    pete is the partner of olga.
    the age of pete is 37.
    child_1 is a dependent child of olga.
    child_2 is a dependent child of olga.
    child_3 is a dependent child of olga.
    child_4 is a dependent child of olga.
    child_5 is a dependent child of olga.
    the age of child_1 is 2.
    the age of child_2 is 5.
    the age of child_3 is 8.
    the age of child_4 is 11.
    the age of child_5 is 14.
    olga receives child benefit for child_1.
    olga receives child benefit for child_2.
    olga receives child benefit for child_3.
    olga receives child benefit for child_4.
    olga receives child benefit for child_5.
    olga receives 427.48 a month as "child benefit".
    pete receives 2500 a month as "wages".
    pete pays 300 a month in income tax and national insurance.
    olga is a householder.
    the monthly rent or mortgage payment of olga is 1200.
    olga holds 500 as "savings".
    result expects answers ["the means test result of olga is not eligible: gross income over the limit under regulation 7(4)"].
    eligible expects answers [].
    gross_income expects answers ["the gross income of olga is 2927.48"].
    gross_income_limit expects answers ["the gross income limit of olga is 2879"].
    disposable_income expects answers ["the disposable income of olga is 0"].
    disposable_capital expects answers ["the disposable capital of olga is 500"].

% ================================================================ queries

query result is:
    the means test result of which client is which result under which provision.
query eligible is:
    which client is financially eligible.
query gross_income is:
    the gross income of which client is which amount.
query gross_income_limit is:
    the gross income limit of which client is which amount.
query disposable_income is:
    the disposable income of which client is which amount.
query disposable_capital is:
    the disposable capital of which client is which amount.
query pensioner_disregard is:
    the pensioner disregard of which client is which amount.
query income_contribution is:
    the assessed monthly income contribution of which client is which amount.
query capital_contribution is:
    the assessed capital contribution of which client is which amount.
query income_contribution_payable is:
    the monthly income contribution payable by which client is which amount.
query capital_contribution_payable is:
    the capital contribution payable by which client is which amount.
